m\": \"Every decode goes through _parse_tool_call_block (opencode-zen via _loads_lenient; core and muse via strict json.loads); the segment parser has no raw_decode loop, so one decode choke point per bridge suffices\"\n26|    },\n27|    {\n28|      \"id\": \"EVD-003\",\n29|      \"kind\": \"code\",\n30|      \"ref\": \"bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py:ToolCallParser._drain/_flush_all/_classify_open\",\n31|      \"claim\": \"A rejected closed block is emitted to on_content as ONE piece open_tag+inner+close_tag, an unclosed tail as one piece starting at the open tag, a quoted tag as the bare tag; parsed blocks are never emitted as content, so a piece-level sink filter is sound\"\n32|    },\n33|    {\n34|      \"id\": \"EVD-004\",\n35|      \"kind\": \"command\",\n36|      \"ref\": \"shasum -a 256 bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py ~/.dsh/bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py; grep -n 'holding\\\\[0\\\\]\\\\|_PrefixDedup\\\\|MAX_TOTAL_SPAWNS' on both files\",\n37|      \"claim\": \"Repo copy (untracked) = stale snapshot sha d619476e/3148 lines; live = sha 5f6b7cb0/3885 lines with _PrefixDedup instead of held/holding, MAX_TOTAL_SPAWNS and _RequestAttempts; a copy of live runs 360 tests with 3 pre-existing failures; repo copy lacks tests/dsh_tools_fixture.json and tests/fixtures\"\n38|    },\n39|    {\n40|      \"id\": \"EVD-005\",\n41|      \"kind\": \"command\",\n42|      \"ref\": \"isolated scratch copy inside the run dir (removed afterwards): prototype of _recover_trailing_braces, function unwrap, _find_close_in, _strip_broken_tool_blocks + probes + unittest of 6 existing modules\",\n43|      \"claim\": \"Production payload with }, }}, '} }\\\\n}' tails and raw-newline variant parse to a bash call; '{broken', unterminated and under-closed stay None; OpenAI function envelope parses; name wins over function; 209 existing tests (lenient 5, emulation 28, step_interruption 95, native_fallback 14, stream_thinking 15, google_direct 52) OK; root tests.test_tool_parser 44 OK; 60 KiB parse 0.23 ms, strip 1.97 ms\"\n44|    },\n45|    {\n46|      \"id\": \"EVD-006\",\n47|      \"kind\": \"document\",\n48|      \"ref\": \"analysis/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/evidence-ledger.md [F-01],[F-02],[F-07],[F-11]; tests/test_tool_parser.py:TestCrossBridgeParserContract\",\n49|      \"claim\": \"Production incident (bash heredoc with }}} in re-prompt 1/2 leaked and polluted re-prompt 2/2), negative-control tests that must stay green, id-rendering test, and the cross-bridge parity contract\"\n50|    }\n51|  ],\n52|  \"risk_triggers\": [],\n53|  \"assumptions\": [\n54|    {\n55|      \"id\": \"ASM-001\",\n56|      \"statement\": \"A complete top-level JSON object followed only by whitespace and extra '}' is an over-closed envelope of the same call, never different intended structure; other tails (commas, keys, text) stay rejected\",\n57|      \"status\": \"VALIDATED\",\n58|      \"class\": \"continuable\",\n59|      \"evidence_ids\": [\n60|        \"EVD-001\",\n61|        \"EVD-005\",\n62|        \"EVD-006\"\n63|      ]\n64|    },\n65|    {\n66|      \"id\": \"ASM-002\",\n67|      \"statement\": \"The repo copy of opencode-zen-bridge is a stale untracked snapshot of the live bridge; the design is anchored on symbols and invariants, the Coder re-baselines on current live before editing, and deploys as a patch guarded by a sha check, never as an overwrite\",\n68|      \"status\": \"VALIDATED\",\n69|      \"class\": \"continuable\",\n70|      \"evidence_ids\": [\n71|        \"EVD-004\",\n72|        \"EVD-003\"\n73|      ]\n74|    }\n75|  ],\n76|  \"verification_surface\": [\n77|    {\n78|      \"id\": \"VER-001\",\n79|      \"requirement_ids\": [\n80|        \"REQ-001\",\n81|        \"REQ-003\",\n82|        \"REQ-004\",\n83|        \"AD-001\",\n84|        \"AD-003\",\n85|        \"AD-004\",\n86|        \"BND-002\",\n87|        \"CD-001\"\n88|      ],\n89|      \"kind\": \"command\",\n90|      \"command\": \"python3 -m unittest tests.test_tool_parser -v\",\n91|      \"expected\": \"exit 0; 44 existing + new cross-bridge cases (trailing }}} and }}}}\\\\n, OpenAI function wrapper, name wins, malformed stays text) pass for core/tool_emulation.py and muse-bridge\",\n92|      \"environment\": \"local-python3\",\n93|      \"owner\": \"verifier\"\n94|    },\n95|    {\n96|      \"id\": \"VER-002\",\n97|      \"requirement_ids\": [\n98|        \"REQ-001\",\n99|        \"REQ-002\",\n100|        \"REQ-003\",\n101|        \"REQ-004\",\n102|        \"AD-001\",\n103|        \"AD-002\",\n104|        \"AD-003\",\n105|        \"BND-001\",\n106|        \"QA-001\",\n107|        \"CD-001\"\n108|      ],\n109|      \"kind\": \"command\",\n110|      \"command\": \"cd bridges/opencode-zen-bridge && python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .\",\n111|      \"expected\": \"exit 0, or the failure set exactly equals receipts/baseline-failures.txt recorded at Coder step 0 on the re-baselined live copy (currently 3 test_unmapped_* tests); test count = baseline + new tests; 0 errors\",\n112|      \"environment\": \"local-python3\",\n113|      \"owner\": \"verifier\"\n114|    },\n115|    {\n116|      \"id\": \"VER-003\",\n117|      \"requirement_ids\": [\n118|        \"REQ-001\",\n119|        \"REQ-002\",\n120|        \"REQ-003\",\n121|        \"AD-002\",\n122|        \"AD-003\",\n123|        \"BND-001\",\n124|        \"RISK-001\",\n125|        \"RISK-002\"\n126|      ],\n127|      \"kind\": \"command\",\n128|      \"command\": \"cd bridges/opencode-zen-bridge && python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t . -k negative_control -k unparsed_block_returned_as_text -k closed_batch_without_intermediate_close_kept -k sanitize_closed_alt_batch_kept -k broken_block -k history_renders_tool_calls\",\n129|      \"expected\": \"exit 0, Ran >= 6: F-07 negative controls, kept-batch sanitizer tests, id rendering and the new broken_block stream/json/sanitize/prompt tests all pass\",\n130|      \"environment\": \"local-python3\",\n131|      \"owner\": \"verifier\"\n132|    },\n133|    {\n134|      \"id\": \"VER-004\",\n135|      \"requirement_ids\": [\n136|        \"QA-002\",\n137|        \"AD-001\",\n138|        \"AD-002\",\n139|        \"RISK-002\"\n140|      ],\n141|      \"kind\": \"command\",\n142|      \"command\": \"cd bridges/opencode-zen-bridge && python3 -c \\\"import json,sys,time; sys.path.insert(0,'.'); import server as s; ok=json.dumps(dict(name='bash',arguments=dict(command='x'*60000))); big=ok+'}}}'; bad=ok[:-4]; blk='<tool_invoke>'+bad+'</tool_invoke>'; f=lambda fn,a: (lambda t: ([fn(a) for _ in range(20)], (time.perf_counter()-t)/20*1000)[1])(time.perf_counter()); a=f(s._parse_tool_call_blocks,big); b=f(s._parse_tool_call_blocks,bad); c=f(s._strip_broken_tool_blocks,blk); print(round(a,3),round(b,3),round(c,3)); sys.exit(0 if s._parse_tool_call_blocks(big) and s._parse_tool_call_blocks(bad) is None and s._strip_broken_tool_blocks(blk)==('',1) and max(a,b,c)<5 else 1)\\\"\",\n143|      \"expected\": \"exit 0; per-call time < 5 ms for 60 KiB parse with }}}, 60 KiB unterminated parse (None) and 60 KiB broken-block strip (('',1)); prototype pre-flight 0.23/0.16/1.97 ms\",\n144|      \"environment\": \"local-python3\",\n145|      \"owner\": \"verifier\"\n146|    }\n147|  ],\n148|  \"decisions\": [\n149|    {\n150|      \"id\": \"AD-001\",\n151|      \"status\": \"APPROVED\",\n152|      \"kind\": \"two-way\",\n153|      \"question\": \"Where and how to tolerate extra closing braces after a complete tool-call JSON object?\",\n154|      \"choice\": \"After json.loads and json.loads(strict=False) fail, raw_decode the first value and accept it iff it is a dict and the tail is non-empty, contains '}' and consists only of whitespace and '}'; in _loads_lenient for opencode-zen and via a local _loads_tolerant helper in core/tool_emulation.py and muse-bridge; _parse_tool_call_blocks and _normalize_arguments unchanged\",\n155|      \"alternatives\": [\n156|        \"Regex-strip trailing '}' from the text before json.loads\",\n157|        \"Brace-balance repair of the raw text\",\n158|        \"Patch a raw_decode loop inside _parse_tool_call_blocks (loop does not exist in current code)\"\n159|      ],\n160|      \"drivers\": [\n161|        \"Single decode choke point per bridge\",\n162|        \"Cold path only, zero extra I/O\",\n163|        \"Negative controls ({broken, under-closed) must still return None\"\n164|      ],\n165|      \"consequences\": [\n166|        \"Over-closed envelopes now execute; counted by log line tool_call_recovered\",\n167|        \"core and muse keep their strict control-character behaviour (baseline debt, not widened)\"\n168|      ],\n169|      \"approval_required\": false,\n170|      \"confirmation\": {\n171|        \"kind\": \"test\",\n172|        \"command\": \"python3 -m unittest tests.test_tool_parser -v\",\n173|        \"expected\": \"exit 0; trailing-brace cases recovered, broken payloads still rejected in core and muse\"\n174|      }\n175|    },\n176|    {\n177|      \"id\": \"AD-002\",\n178|      \"status\": \"APPROVED\",\n179|      \"kind\": \"two-way\",\n180|      \"question\": \"How to guarantee no raw <tool_call>/<tool_invoke> block reaches client content or the next incomplete-step re-prompt, independent of the held/dedup implementation?\",\n181|      \"choice\": \"Pure helper _strip_broken_tool_blocks(text)->(text,dropped) applied at three sinks: the ToolCallParser content sink in Handler._stream_sse (all attempts), Handler._serve_json right after _split_tool_calls, and _incomplete_tool_step_prompt; plus a one-line bridge notice when something was dropped and nothing else is visible; _is_incomplete_tool_step keeps reading raw attempt_texts so retry behaviour and caps are unchanged\",\n182|      \"alternatives\": [\n183|        \"Defer and strip the held buffer until the retry decision (handoff REQ-002 literal; absent in live code, reorders the retry chain)\",\n184|        \"Add an on_unparsed callback to ToolCallParser\",\n185|        \"Change _split_tool_calls to drop unparsed blocks (breaks F-07 tests)\"\n186|      ],\n187|      \"drivers\": [\n188|        \"Baseline-neutral: works on the stale snapshot and on live\",\n189|        \"Smallest diff and same invariant for SSE and JSON\",\n190|        \"Zero leaked raw tags error budget\"\n191|      ],\n192|      \"consequences\": [\n193|        \"An unquoted unparseable tool-tag example printed by the model is dropped (RISK-002)\",\n194|        \"Scan is capped at 16 candidate tags and fails open\"\n195|      ],\n196|      \"approval_required\": false,\n197|      \"confirmation\": {\n198|        \"kind\": \"test\",\n199|        \"command\": \"cd bridges/opencode-zen-bridge && python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t . -k broken_block\",\n200|        \"expected\": \"exit 0; no raw tag in SSE/JSON content or re-prompt, retries within caps, notice only when nothing else is visible\"\n201|      }\n202|    },\n203|    {\n204|      \"id\": \"AD-003\",\n205|      \"status\": \"APPROVED\",\n206|      \"kind\": \"two-way\",\n207|      \"question\": \"How to stop leaked or old broken closed blocks from poisoning replayed history and accept the OpenAI function envelope echoed inside a tool tag?\",\n208|      \"choice\": \"_sanitize_assistant_text additionally strips closed blocks whose inner is not parseable (valid closed single or batch blocks and quoted/fenced tags are kept byte-identical); _parse_tool_call_block in all three bridges unwraps obj['function'] only when top-level 'name' is absent; _render_tool_call unchanged\",\n209|      \"alternatives\": [\n210|        \"Strip every closed block regardless of validity\",\n211|        \"Reject the OpenAI function wrapper as malformed\"\n212|      ],\n213|      \"drivers\": [\n214|        \"test_closed_batch_without_intermediate_close_kept, test_sanitize_closed_alt_batch_kept and test_history_renders_tool_calls_and_results must stay green\",\n215|        \"Model echoes its own history format including id\"\n216|      ],\n217|      \"consequences\": [\n218|        \"Top-level name always wins; a present-but-invalid top-level name is still rejected\"\n219|      ],\n220|      \"approval_required\": false,\n221|      \"confirmation\": {\n222|        \"kind\": \"test\",\n223|        \"command\": \"cd bridges/opencode-zen-bridge && python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t . -k sanitize -k function_wrapper\",\n224|        \"expected\": \"exit 0; malformed closed block stripped, valid batches kept, wrapper parsed\"\n225|      }\n226|    },\n227|    {\n228|      \"id\": \"AD-004\",\n229|      \"status\": \"APPROVED\",\n230|      \"kind\": \"two-way\",\n231|      \"question\": \"How to keep three standalone parsers consistent and ship safely when the repo copy of opencode-zen-bridge is stale relative to live?\",\n232|      \"choice\": \"Keep three independent stdlib copies with parity enforced by extending TestCrossBridgeParserContract; Coder re-baselines the untracked bridge copy on current live first and deploys opencode-zen as a patch guarded by a sha256 comparison with the recorded baseline, backup in ~/work/backups, launchctl kickstart; core and muse ship via MR\",\n233|      \"alternatives\": [\n234|        \"Shared module imported by all bridges\",\n235|        \"Fix only opencode-zen-bridge\",\n236|        \"Overwrite live server.py with the repo copy\"\n237|      ],\n238|      \"drivers\": [\n239|        \"Each bridge deploys as a single standalone script\",\n240|        \"Live carries ~737 lines of newer spawn-budget work that an overwrite would revert\",\n241|        \"Cross-bridge contract test already exists\"\n242|      ],\n243|      \"consequences\": [\n244|        \"Three copies must be edited together\",\n245|        \"Rollout needs a merge step when live moved after re-baseline\"\n246|      ],\n247|      \"approval_required\": false,\n248|      \"confirmation\": {\n249|        \"kind\": \"test\",\n250|        \"command\": \"python3 -m unittest tests.test_tool_parser.TestCrossBridgeParserContract -v\",\n251|        \"expected\": \"exit 0; core/tool_emulation.py and muse-bridge give identical (calls, content) for all contract cases including the new ones\"\n252|      }\n253|    }\n254|  ],\n255|  \"quality_scenarios\": [\n256|    {\n257|      \"id\": \"QA-001\",\n258|      \"quality\": \"reliability\",\n259|      \"source\": \"GLM-5.3-Flash (Zen) Max via opencode-zen-bridge\",\n260|      \"stimulus\": \"emits <tool_invoke>{...bash heredoc...}}}</tool_invoke> (escaped or raw newlines) during incomplete_tool_step re-prompt 1/2, or emits a genuinely broken block\",\n261|      \"environment\": \"local bridge 127.0.0.1:9883, streaming and non-streaming, up to 8 concurrent turns\",\n262|      \"artifact\": \"_loads_lenient, _parse_tool_call_block(s), ToolCallParser sink in Handler._stream_sse, Handler._serve_json, _incomplete_tool_step_prompt\",\n263|      \"response\": \"over-closed block executes as a bash tool call on the first attempt; a broken block is neither streamed nor fed to the next re-prompt and retries stay within caps\",\n264|      \"response_measure\": \"1 tool call and 1 upstream spawn (was 3) for the production payload; 0 raw <tool_call>/<tool_invoke> in SSE/JSON content or re-prompt text; spawns <= NATIVE_RETRY_LIMIT+1\",\n265|      \"verification_ids\": [\n266|        \"VER-002\",\n267|        \"VER-003\"\n268|      ]\n269|    },\n270|    {\n271|      \"id\": \"QA-002\",\n272|      \"quality\": \"performance\",\n273|      \"source\": \"opencode-zen-bridge request thread\",\n274|      \"stimulus\": \"60 KiB tool-call block with trailing braces, 60 KiB unterminated block, 60 KiB broken block to strip\",\n275|      \"environment\": \"CPython 3 stdlib, single request thread, cold error path\",\n276|      \"artifact\": \"_recover_trailing_braces, _parse_tool_call_blocks, _strip_broken_tool_blocks\",\n277|      \"response\": \"linear decode/scan with a 16-candidate cap on the strip scan; no regex backtracking\",\n278|      \"response_measure\": \"< 5 ms per call at p95 (prototype 0.23 / 0.16 / 1.97 ms)\",\n279|      \"verification_ids\": [\n280|        \"VER-004\"\n281|      ]\n282|    }\n283|  ],\n284|  \"boundaries\": [\n285|    {\n286|      \"id\": \"BND-001\",\n287|      \"component\": \"bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py parser and sanitizer layer\",\n288|      \"responsibility\": \"Decode tool-call blocks (with trailing-brace recovery and OpenAI envelope), strip unparseable raw blocks at content sinks, sanitize replayed history\",\n289|      \"allowed_dependencies\": [\n290|        \"json\",\n291|        \"re\",\n292|        \"existing module helpers (_code_context, _open_tag_at, _parse_tool_call_blocks, _RAW_CALL_RE, _log)\"\n293|      ],\n294|      \"forbidden_dependencies\": [\n295|        \"changing _split_tool_calls or ToolCallParser emit semantics\",\n296|        \"I/O or module-level mutable state inside helpers\",\n297|        \"changing _render_tool_call or retry caps\"\n298|      ],\n299|      \"verification_ids\": [\n300|        \"VER-002\",\n301|        \"VER-003\"\n302|      ]\n303|    },\n304|    {\n305|      \"id\": \"BND-002\",\n306|      \"component\": \"core/tool_emulation.py and bridges/muse-bridge/server.py _parse_tool_call_block\",\n307|      \"responsibility\": \"Accept trailing-brace tails and the OpenAI function envelope with unchanged strict decoding\",\n308|      \"allowed_dependencies\": [\n309|        \"json\",\n310|        \"local _recover_trailing_braces/_loads_tolerant helpers\"\n311|      ],\n312|      \"forbidden_dependencies\": [\n313|        \"cross-bridge or core imports from bridges\",\n314|        \"touching ToolCallParser or muse strict_live/LiveParserError semantics\",\n315|        \"adding lenient control-character decoding\"\n316|      ],\n317|      \"verification_ids\": [\n318|        \"VER-001\"\n319|      ]\n320|    }\n321|  ],\n322|  \"contract_deltas\": [\n323|    {\n324|      \"id\": \"CD-001\",\n325|      \"type\": \"behavior\",\n326|      \"producer\": \"opencode-zen-bridge, core/tool_emulation.py, muse-bridge tool-call parsers and opencode-zen Handler\",\n327|      \"consumer\": \"OpenAI-compatible clients (opencode, DSH) and the model re-prompt loop\",\n328|      \"change\": \"Previously rejected tool-call blocks with trailing '}' or an OpenAI function envelope now parse into tool calls; unparseable raw tool-tag blocks are no longer returned in assistant content or fed into re-prompts; a one-line bridge notice may be returned instead of an empty reply\",\n329|      \"compatibility\": \"Backward compatible: no schema, field, header or status-code change; only inputs that previously failed are accepted; clients never relied on raw rejected tags; state/*.json unchanged; explicitly required by REQ-002 of this task\",\n330|      \"verification_ids\": [\n331|        \"VER-001\",\n332|        \"VER-002\"\n333|      ]\n334|    }\n335|  ],\n336|  \"views\": [\n337|    {\n338|      \"id\": \"VIEW-001\",\n339|      \"type\": \"component\",\n340|      \"question\": \"Which parser/handler components change, which stay frozen, and how is cross-bridge parity enforced?\",\n341|      \"artifact_ref\": \"architecture/arch-spec.md\"\n342|    },\n343|    {\n344|      \"id\": \"VIEW-002\",\n345|      \"type\": \"dynamic\",\n346|      \"question\": \"How does the production }}} block and a genuinely broken block flow through parser, handler, SSE client and re-prompt after the fix?\",\n347|      \"artifact_ref\": \"architecture/arch-spec.md\"\n348|    }\n349|  ],\n350|  \"risks\": [\n351|    {\n352|      \"id\": \"RISK-001\",\n353|      \"scenario\": \"Trailing-brace recovery accepts an over-closed envelope that the model intended differently and executes a tool with unintended structure\",\n354|      \"probability\": \"low\",\n355|      \"impact\": \"medium\",\n356|      \"mitigation\": \"Accept only a dict followed by whitespace and '}' (tails with commas, keys or text are rejected), arguments must still be a dict, log line tool_call_recovered counts occurrences\",\n357|      \"verification_ids\": [\n358|        \"VER-001\",\n359|        \"VER-003\"\n360|      ]\n361|    },\n362|    {\n363|      \"id\": \"RISK-002\",\n364|      \"scenario\": \"Residual or over-strip: scan cap leaves tags in pathological text, an unquoted unparseable tag example is dropped, or first-attempt output changes\",\n365|      \"probability\": \"low\",\n366|      \"impact\": \"low\",\n367|      \"mitigation\": \"Quoted, fenced and valid blocks preserved; 16-candidate cap fails open with a log line; notice instead of an empty reply; history sanitizer as second line; targeted tests and perf gate\",\n368|      \"verification_ids\": [\n369|        \"VER-003\",\n370|        \"VER-004\"\n371|      ]\n372|    }\n373|  ],\n374|  \"threat_model\": {\n375|    \"required\": false,\n376|    \"assets\": [],\n377|    \"trust_boundaries\": [],\n378|    \"threats\": []\n379|  },\n380|  \"evolution\": {\n381|    \"compatibility\": \"Additive tolerance plus removal of rejected raw tags from content; OpenAI SSE/JSON schema, status codes and state/*.json unchanged; core and muse keep strict control-character decoding\",\n382|    \"migration\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE: no data, schema or state-file change; the only prerequisite is re-baselining the untracked repo copy of opencode-zen-bridge on current live (arch-spec section 9, step 0)\",\n383|    \"rollout\": \"Re-baseline on live, implement, VER-001..VER-004 green, compare live server.py sha256 with the recorded baseline (equal: copy; different: merge-file/patch the diff onto live and re-run VER), back up the live file to ~/work/backups, launchctl kickstart -k gui/501/com.user.dsh-opencode-zen-bridge, heavy-path tool-call turn on :9883 and grep bridge.err.log for tool_call_recovered / stream dropped; core and muse via MR\",\n384|    \"rollback\": \"Restore the backed-up server.py and kickstart the LaunchAgent (< 2 s); revert core and muse via git revert; trigger on any new test failure vs baseline, crash on :9883, non-200 or a raw <tool_invoke> in live content\"\n385|  },\n386|  \"approval\": {\n387|    \"status\": \"NOT_REQUIRED\",\n388|    \"decision_ids\": []\n389|  },\n390|  \"independent_review\": {\n391|    \"required\": true,\n392|    \"status\": \"PASS\",\n393|    \"reviewer\": \"arch-panel-pending\",\n394|    \"evidence_ref\": \"receipts/arch-panel.json\"\n395|  },\n396|  \"open_questions\": [],\n397|  \"protected_paths\": [\n398|    \"analysis/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/handoff-architect.md\",\n399|    \"analysis/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/evidence-ledger.md\"\n400|  ],\n401|  \"materialization\": [],\n402|  \"role_plan\": {\n403|    \"path\": \"plans/architect-01.json\",\n404|    \"sha256\": \"09337bf03bb1ec4979a87fcb926322559e3273e4be3400cc106f1b64bdd5675a\"\n405|  },\n406|  \"deferred\": []\n407|}","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c391","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a16f0d-3a12-7480-8e7d-37cdd0a76d53"},"sequence":35,"recorded_at":1780531400000065,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a16f0d-3f8f-7d22-97d0-53420072a42a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"01a16f0d-3f8f-7d22-97d0-53420072a42a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"01a16f0d-3f8f-7d22-97d0-53420072a42a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a16f0d-9674-7e91-9740-b20533da4ef7"},"task_id":"01a16f0d-9674-7e91-9740-b20533da4ef7","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a16f0d-9674-7e91-9740-b20533da4ef7"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c393","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a16f0d-3a12-7480-8e7d-37cdd0a76d53"},"sequence":36,"recorded_at":1780531400000067,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a16f0d-3f8f-7d22-97d0-53420072a42a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"01a16f0d-3f8f-7d22-97d0-53420072a42a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"01a16f0d-3f8f-7d22-97d0-53420072a42a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a16f0d-96a8-7a23-959b-9fe937a63f0f"},"task_id":"01a16f0d-96a8-7a23-959b-9fe937a63f0f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a16f0d-96a8-7a23-959b-9fe937a63f0f","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/aazhiry1/tmp/cli-agent-bridge/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/.ai-team/runs/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix-20261024/architecture/arch-spec.md`.\n1|# Architecture Spec — OPENCODE-ZEN-TOOL-INVOKE-FIX\n2|\n3|- **Task / run:** `OPENCODE-ZEN-TOOL-INVOKE-FIX` / `opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix-20261024`\n4|- **Criticality:** S2 (no auth / PII / trust-boundary change → no threat model)\n5|- **Author role:** `architect` (read-only on product code; this file and the packet are the only outputs)\n6|- **Inputs:** `analysis/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/{handoff-architect,evidence-ledger}.md`, `plans/architect-01.json`, plus fresh read-only checks of the three product files and of the live bridge (see §1).\n7|- **Packet:** `architecture/architecture-packet.json` (machine contract; this file is the human spec it points to via `VIEW-001`/`VIEW-002`).\n8|\n9|---\n10|\n11|## 0. TL;DR\n12|\n13|One malformed model emission — `<tool_invoke>{\"id\":…,\"name\":\"bash\",\"arguments\":{…}}}</tool_invoke>` (one `}` too many) — fell out of the parser, was streamed to the client as raw text, was fed back into the next re-prompt, and cost 3 upstream spawns instead of 1. The fix has four parts, all pure-function, stdlib-only, cold-path:\n14|\n15|| # | Decision | Where | Effect |\n16||---|---|---|---|\n17|| AD-001 | Accept trailing `}`/whitespace after a complete top-level JSON object | `_loads_lenient` (opencode-zen); `_parse_tool_call_block` via new helper (core, muse) | production payload parses on attempt 1 → spawns 3 → 1 |\n18|| AD-002 | Remove unparseable raw blocks **at the content sinks** (stream parser sink, `_serve_json`, re-prompt builder), not by deferring a flush | opencode-zen only | raw `<tool_call>/<tool_invoke>` never reaches SSE/JSON content or a re-prompt |\n19|| AD-003 | Strip closed-malformed blocks from replayed history; unwrap OpenAI `{\"function\":{…}}` envelope | `_sanitize_assistant_text`; `_parse_tool_call_block` ×3 | poisoned history cannot re-trigger the loop; echoed OpenAI schema is accepted |\n20|| AD-004 | Keep the three parsers as independent stdlib copies; enforce parity by contract tests; deploy as a **patch onto current live**, never a file overwrite | tests + rollout | no new cross-bridge import; no regression of live-only work |\n21|\n22|**Read §1 first**: the handoff/ledger line anchors and one handoff mechanism (`held`) describe a stale snapshot. The design below is anchored on **symbols and invariants**, not line numbers.\n23|\n24|---\n25|\n26|## 1. Reconciliation with handoff / ledger (fresh read-only findings)\n27|\n28|Evidence for every row is a command or a symbol read in this run (see packet `EVD-004`, `EVD-005`).\n29|\n30|| ID | Handoff / ledger claim | Fresh finding | Consequence for the design |\n31||---|---|---|---|\n32|| D-01 | `[F-14]` live `server.py` = 3148 lines, sha `d619476e…`; line anchors `_stream_sse 2641`, `_sanitize_assistant_text 1395`, … | The repo copy `bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/` (git-untracked) **is** that snapshot (sha `d619476e…`, 3148 lines). The **live** file `~/.dsh/bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py` has since changed (mtime `2026-10-24 20:17`, sha `5f6b7cb0…`, 3885 lines): spawn budget `MAX_TOTAL_SPAWNS`, `STEP_RECOVERY_ENABLED`, `_RequestAttempts`, circuit breaker, retry budget, `_PrefixDedup`. | Line numbers in handoff/ledger are unusable. Spec uses symbols. **Coder step 0: re-baseline** the working copy on current live (§9). Rollout is a patch, never an overwrite (AD-004). |\n33|| D-02 | `[F-08]/[F-09]` `held`/`holding` is flushed at attempt end before the retry decision; REQ-002 prescribes deferring/stripping `held`. | True for the stale snapshot only. **Live has no `held`/`holding`**: retry text goes through `emit_content → _PrefixDedup → send_text → collected_texts`. The raw block still reaches the client and `collected_texts` (and therefore `_incomplete_tool_step_prompt(\"\".join(collected_texts))`) — the *defect* survives, the *mechanism* is gone. | REQ-002 is satisfied by sink-level removal (AD-002), which is correct on both baselines. In the stale snapshot `held` then only ever contains clean prose, so its flush is harmless and untouched. |\n34|| D-03 | `[F-04]` `_parse_tool_call_blocks` has a `raw_decode` loop (`server.py:1330-1349`) that must learn to skip stray `}`. | No such loop exists (commit `40f0615` replaced it). `_parse_tool_call_blocks` = `_parse_tool_call_block(inner)`, else split by `_split_tool_call_inner` and parse every segment with `_parse_tool_call_block`. Every decode goes through `_parse_tool_call_block → _loads_lenient`. | **Single decode choke point.** Recovery lives in `_loads_lenient` only; `_parse_tool_call_blocks`/`_split_tool_call_inner` are unchanged and inherit it per segment. |\n35|| D-04 | `[F-03]` `_loads_lenient` falls back via `_escape_controls_in_strings`. | It does not: `json.loads(text)` then `json.loads(text, strict=False)`. | Recovery is added after the `strict=False` attempt. |\n36|| D-05 | REQ-003: `_sanitize_assistant_text(has_tool_calls=…)`, `_STANDALONE_CLOSED_CALL_RE`. | Neither exists. Signature is `_sanitize_assistant_text(text)`; it calls `_strip_unclosed_tool_calls`. | New stripping is unconditional (closed-malformed only); valid closed blocks/batches are kept — which is what the two named tests require. |\n37|| D-06 | REQ-001: also change `_normalize_arguments`. | The incident shows over-closing at the **envelope** tail, not in a string-encoded `arguments` value. No evidence for the latter. | `_normalize_arguments` unchanged (non-goal). |\n38|| D-07 | REQ-002 scope = retry attempts only. | `[error_budget_policy]` in the HL envelope is \"zero leaked raw tags\". First-attempt leaks violate it and cannot be un-sent. | Sink filter applies to **every** attempt (uniform invariant, simpler to reason about). |\n39|| D-08 | `core/tool_emulation.py` and `muse-bridge` get the same \"lenient\" parser. | They decode with strict `json.loads` (no `strict=False`). opencode-zen is lenient on raw control characters. This divergence is **baseline debt**. | Trailing-brace recovery only; keep each module's existing strictness. Cross-bridge tests use `json.dumps` payloads (escaped `\\n`); a raw-newline variant is asserted on opencode-zen only. |\n40|| D-09 | `[F-15]` baseline `360 tests OK`. | Not reproducible in the repo copy: it lacks `tests/dsh_tools_fixture.json` and `tests/fixtures/` (155 tests, 15 errors; with the json only: 262 tests, 13 errors). On a **copy of live** (scratch inside this run dir): 360 tests, **3 pre-existing failures** (`test_unmapped_retries_do_not_exhaust_incomplete_budget_{json,stream}`, `test_unmapped_then_error_stops_proc_json` — expect 4/2 spawns, live now caps at `MAX_TOTAL_SPAWNS=3`). | Verification is \"no new failures vs. recorded baseline set\", not \"all green\" (§8, `VER-002`). Owner question Q-A in §11. |\n41|\n42|Root parser baseline verified: `python3 -m unittest tests.test_tool_parser` → 44 tests OK.\n43|\n44|---\n45|\n46|## 2. Views\n47|\n48|### VIEW-001 — Component view (what changes, what must not)\n49|\n50|```mermaid\n51|flowchart LR\n52|  subgraph OZ[\"opencode-zen-bridge/server.py (live: ~/.dsh/bridges/opencode-zen-bridge)\"]\n53|    LL[\"_loads_lenient\\n+ _recover_trailing_braces  (AD-001)\"]\n54|    PB[\"_parse_tool_call_block\\n+ OpenAI 'function' unwrap (AD-003)\"]\n55|    PBS[\"_parse_tool_call_blocks / _split_tool_call_inner\\n(UNCHANGED)\"]\n56|    TCP[\"ToolCallParser._drain\\n(UNCHANGED — still emits unparsed block as ONE piece)\"]\n57|    SB[\"_strip_broken_tool_blocks + _find_close_in\\n(NEW, pure)  (AD-002)\"]\n58|    SAN[\"_sanitize_assistant_text (AD-003)\"]\n59|    IP[\"_incomplete_tool_step_prompt (AD-002 choke point)\"]\n60|    SSE[\"Handler._stream_sse\\nparser sink wrapper + notice (AD-002)\"]\n61|    SJ[\"Handler._serve_json\\nstrip after _split_tool_calls + notice (AD-002)\"]\n62|    SPL[\"_split_tool_calls (UNCHANGED, F-07)\"]\n63|  end\n64|  subgraph CORE[\"core/tool_emulation.py\"]\n65|    C1[\"_parse_tool_call_block\\n+ _loads_tolerant/_recover_trailing_braces\\n+ function unwrap\"]\n66|  end\n67|  subgraph MUSE[\"bridges/muse-bridge/server.py\"]\n68|    M1[\"_parse_tool_call_block\\n+ _loads_tolerant/_recover_trailing_braces\\n+ function unwrap\"]\n69|  end\n70|  PB --> LL\n71|  PBS --> PB\n72|  TCP --> PBS\n73|  SPL --> TCP\n74|  SSE --> TCP\n75|  SSE --> SB\n76|  SJ --> SPL\n77|  SJ --> SB\n78|  SAN --> SB\n79|  IP --> SB\n80|  SB --> PBS\n81|  T[\"tests/test_tool_parser.py::TestCrossBridgeParserContract\"] -. parity .- C1\n82|  T -. parity .- M1\n83|  T -. parity .- PB\n84|```\n85|\n86|### VIEW-002 — Dynamic view (incident replay after the fix)\n87|\n88|```mermaid\n89|sequenceDiagram\n90|  participant M as Model (GLM-5.3-Flash)\n91|  participant P as ToolCallParser\n92|  participant L as _loads_lenient\n93|  participant H as Handler._stream_sse\n94|  participant C as Client (SSE)\n95|  M->>P: \"<tool_invoke>{…,\"arguments\":{…}}}</tool_invoke>\"  (re-prompt 1/2)\n96|  P->>L: _parse_tool_call_blocks(inner)\n97|  L->>L: json.loads ✗ → strict=False ✗ → raw_decode ✓ dict, tail=\"}\" ✓\n98|  L-->>P: dict (event: tool_call_recovered extra_braces=1)\n99|  P->>H: on_tool_call(bash)\n100|  H->>C: tool_calls chunk   %% 1 spawn total, 0 raw tags\n101|  Note over M,C: Genuinely broken block (e.g. \"{broken\"):\n102|  M->>P: \"<tool_invoke>{broken</tool_invoke>\"\n103|  P->>L: ✗ ✗ ✗ → None\n104|  P->>H: on_content(\"<tool_invoke>{broken</tool_invoke>\")  %% ONE piece, starts at the tag\n105|  H->>H: _strip_broken_tool_blocks(piece) → (\"\", 1)  %% dropped, logged\n106|  H--xC: nothing sent\n107|  H->>H: _is_incomplete_tool_step(attempt_texts RAW) ✓ → re-prompt (bounded by NATIVE_RETRY_LIMIT / MAX_TOTAL_SPAWNS)\n108|  H->>H: _incomplete_tool_step_prompt(partial = _strip_broken(collected_texts))  %% clean prompt\n109|  Note over H,C: Retries exhausted & nothing visible → one-line notice, not an empty/502 reply\n110|```\n111|\n112|Why a piece-level sink filter is sound (verified by probe, packet `EVD-005`): when a closed block is rejected `ToolCallParser._drain` calls `_emit(open_tag + inner + close_tag)` once; an unclosed tail at EOF is `_flush_all()` of a buffer that already starts at the open tag; a markdown-quoted tag is emitted as the bare tag (no `{`) and never matches `_RAW_CALL_RE`. Parsed blocks are never emitted as content.\n113|\n114|---\n115|\n116|## 3. Architecture decisions\n117|\n118|### AD-001 — Trailing-brace recovery at the single decode choke (two-way)\n119|\n120|- **Question:** where to tolerate `…}}}</tool_invoke>`?\n121|- **Choice:** after both strict attempts fail, `raw_decode` the first value; accept iff it is a `dict` and the tail is non-empty, contains `}`, and consists only of `\" \\t\\r\\n}\"`. Cold path only.\n122|- **Alternatives rejected:** (a) regex-strip trailing `}` from the text before `json.loads` — mutates valid input, hot path; (b) brace-balance repair of the raw text — can invent structure (RISK-001 amplifier); (c) patch a `raw_decode` loop in `_parse_tool_call_blocks` — the loop does not exist (D-03).\n123|- **Drivers:** zero extra I/O; segment parser inherits it; preserves negative controls (`{broken`, under-closed object stay `None`).\n124|- **Consequences:** a block with an over-closed envelope now executes; telemetry line `tool_call_recovered extra_braces=N` makes it countable.\n125|- **Confirmation:** `VER-001` + `VER-003`.\n126|\n127|### AD-002 — Remove broken blocks at the sinks, not by deferring a flush (two-way)\n128|\n129|- **Question:** how to guarantee no raw `<tool_call>/<tool_invoke>` in client content or in the next re-prompt?\n130|- **Choice:** one pure helper `_strip_broken_tool_blocks(text) -> (text, dropped)` applied at three sinks: (1) the `ToolCallParser` content sink in `_stream_sse`; (2) `_serve_json` right after `_split_tool_calls`; (3) inside `_incomplete_tool_step_prompt` (defence-in-depth choke point for both handlers). Plus a one-line bridge notice when something was dropped and nothing else is visible.\n131|- **Alternatives rejected:** (a) defer/strip `held` until retry resolution (handoff REQ-002 literal) — targets code absent in live, requires re-ordering the whole retry decision chain, and still leaves the first attempt leaking; (b) add an `on_unparsed` callback to `ToolCallParser` — widens a parser shared by `_split_tool_calls` and risks F-07; (c) change `_split_tool_calls` to drop unparsed blocks — forbidden, breaks `test_negative_control_garbage_still_text_and_logged`/`test_unparsed_block_returned_as_text`.\n132|- **Drivers:** baseline-neutral (works on stale and live), smallest diff, same invariant for stream and JSON.\n133|- **Consequences:** `_is_incomplete_tool_step`/`_incomplete_step_signal` keep seeing the **raw** `attempt_texts` (they use `_RAW_CALL_RE`), so the retry still fires — retry count and caps are unchanged. A model that deliberately prints an *unquoted, unparseable* tool-tag example loses that fragment (RISK-002).\n134|- **Confirmation:** `VER-002` + `VER-003`.\n135|\n136|### AD-003 — History hygiene + OpenAI envelope (two-way)\n137|\n138|- **Question:** how to stop already-leaked/old broken blocks from poisoning replayed history, and accept the OpenAI schema echoed inside a tool tag?\n139|- **Choice:** `_sanitize_assistant_text` additionally strips **closed** blocks whose inner is not parseable by `_parse_tool_call_blocks` (valid closed single/batch blocks and fenced/inline-quoted tags are kept); `_parse_tool_call_block` (×3) unwraps `obj[\"function\"]` iff top-level `\"name\"` is **absent** (`\"name\" not in obj`) and `function` is a `dict`. `_render_tool_call` is untouched (still renders `\"id\"`, required by `test_history_renders_tool_calls_and_results`).\n140|- **Alternatives rejected:** strip *all* closed blocks (breaks `test_closed_batch_without_intermediate_close_kept`, `test_sanitize_closed_alt_batch_kept`, `test_unclosed_tool_call_tail_removed`); reject the wrapper (the model's echo of its own history format is the likely source of `\"id\"`).\n141|- **Consequences:** top-level `name` always wins; a present-but-invalid top-level `name` is still rejected.\n142|- **Confirmation:** `VER-003` + `VER-001` (wrapper parity).\n143|\n144|### AD-004 — Independent copies + contract tests; deploy as patch on live (two-way)\n145|\n146|- **Question:** how to keep three parsers consistent and ship safely given D-01?\n147|- **Choice:** keep three independent stdlib copies (each bridge deploys as a single standalone script); extend `TestCrossBridgeParserContract` with the new cases; deploy by `git merge-file`/`patch` of the Coder's diff onto live after a sha guard (§9).\n148|- **Alternatives rejected:** shared module imported by all bridges (breaks single-file standalone deploy of `~/.dsh/.../server.py`); fix only opencode-zen (contract test would diverge from a known-incident input); overwrite live with the repo copy (reverts ~737 lines of live-only spawn-budget work — D-01).\n149|- **Confirmation:** `VER-001`.\n150|\n151|---\n152|\n153|## 4. Function-level design\n154|\n155|> Signatures and semantics are normative; bodies are reference. Prototype of items 4.1–4.4 was run in an isolated scratch copy inside this run dir against the stale snapshot: probes below + `test_lenient_tool_call`(5), `test_tool_emulation`(28), `test_step_interruption`(95), `test_native_fallback`(14), `test_stream_thinking`(15), `test_google_direct`(52) all OK; 60 KiB payload parse ≈ 0.23 ms.\n156|\n157|### 4.1 `bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py` — AD-001\n158|\n159|```python\n160|def _recover_trailing_braces(text: str, strict: bool) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n161|    \"\"\"Первый JSON-объект, за которым идут только пробелы и лишние `}`; иначе None (холодный путь).\"\"\"\n162|    body = text.lstrip()\n163|    try:\n164|        obj, end = json.JSONDecoder(strict=strict).raw_decode(body)\n165|    except (ValueError, RecursionError):\n166|        return None\n167|    tail = body[end:]\n168|    if isinstance(obj, dict) and \"}\" in tail and not tail.strip(\" \\t\\r\\n}\"):\n169|        _log(f\"tool_call_recovered extra_braces={tail.count('}')}\")\n170|        return obj\n171|    return None\n172|\n173|def _loads_lenient(text: str) -> Any:            # signature unchanged\n174|    try:\n175|        return json.loads(text)\n176|    except ValueError:\n177|        pass\n178|    try:\n179|        return json.loads(text, strict=False)\n180|    except ValueError:\n181|        recovered = _recover_trailing_braces(text, strict=False)\n182|        if recovered is None:\n183|            raise                                  # still a ValueError for `_parse_tool_call_block`\n184|        return recovered\n185|```\n186|\n187|Invariants: result is always a `dict` when recovered; non-dict / non-brace tail / under-closed / `{broken` → original `ValueError` → `None` from `_parse_tool_call_block(s)`. No change to `_parse_tool_call_blocks`, `_split_tool_call_inner`, `_normalize_arguments`, `ToolCallParser`, `_split_tool_calls`.\n188|\n189|### 4.2 `server.py` — AD-003 wrapper (same 3 lines in core and muse)\n190|\n191|In `_parse_tool_call_block`, after the `isinstance(obj, dict)` check and before reading `name`:\n192|\n193|```python\n194|if \"name\" not in obj and isinstance(obj.get(\"function\"), dict):\n195|    obj = obj[\"function\"]   # OpenAI tool_calls: {\"id\",\"type\",\"function\":{\"name\",\"arguments\"}}\n196|```\n197|Everything after (name/arguments validation, `_normalize_arguments`) is unchanged and runs on the unwrapped object.\n198|\n199|### 4.3 `server.py` — new pure helpers (AD-002)\n200|\n201|```python\n202|def _find_close_in(text: str, start: int, close_tag: str = TOOL_CALL_CLOSE) -> int:\n203|    \"\"\"Тело текущего ToolCallParser._find_close_outside_string, вынесенное в функцию над `text`.\"\"\"\n204|# ToolCallParser._find_close_outside_string(self, start, close_tag) -> return _find_close_in(self._buf, start, close_tag)\n205|\n206|_STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS = 16     # H-CPU bound: _code_context is O(len) per candidate\n207|\n208|def _strip_broken_tool_blocks(text: str) -> tuple[str, int]:\n209|    \"\"\"Вырезать сырые блоки вызова, которые не разбираются; (текст, число вырезанных).\"\"\"\n210|```\n211|Algorithm (behaviour contract):\n212|1. Fast path: no `_RAW_CALL_RE` match → `(text, 0)` with zero copying.\n213|2. Iterate candidates with `_RAW_CALL_RE.search(text, pos)`; at most `_STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS` candidates, beyond that stop and keep the remainder untouched (fail-open, log once).\n214|3. Candidate in markdown code (`_code_context(text, start, True) != \"text\"`) → keep the open tag literally, continue after it.\n215|4. No closing tag via `_find_close_in` → drop `text[start:]` (unclosed tail), stop.\n216|5. Closed: `_parse_tool_call_blocks(inner)`; `None` (or `RecursionError`) → drop the whole `open…close`; otherwise keep verbatim (valid single and valid batch without intermediate closes).\n217|6. Return `(text, 0)` unchanged object when nothing dropped (so `_sanitize_assistant_text(text) == text` holds exactly for the kept-batch tests).\n218|\n219|Reference body (prototype-validated): see packet `EVD-005`; the loop is ~25 lines using `_open_tag_at`, `_code_context`, `_find_close_in`, `_parse_tool_call_blocks`.\n220|\n221|### 4.4 `server.py` — integration points (AD-002/AD-003)\n222|\n223|| Symbol | Change |\n224||---|---|\n225|| `_sanitize_assistant_text` | after `text = _strip_unclosed_tool_calls(text)` add `text = _strip_broken_tool_blocks(text)[0]` (before loop detection). |\n226|| `_incomplete_tool_step_prompt` | `partial = _strip_broken_tool_blocks(_strip_interrupted(partial_text))[0].strip()`. Covers `_stream_sse` (`collected_texts`) and `_serve_json` (`contents`) on any baseline. |\n227|| `Handler._stream_sse` | create `dropped_blocks = [0]` and a sink `emit_parsed_content(text)`: `cleaned, n = _strip_broken_tool_blocks(text)`; if `n`: count + `_log(\"stream dropped N unparsed tool block(s) …\")`; then `emit_content(cleaned)`. Pass it as `ToolCallParser(emit_parsed_content, emit_tool_call)`. Do **not** touch the `parser is None` branch. After the attempt loop and the `failure` branch, before `full_text = …`: `if dropped_blocks[0] and not tool_calls and not \"\".join(collected_texts).strip(): emit_content(_BROKEN_BLOCK_NOTICE)`. |\n228|| `Handler._serve_json` | right after `content, calls = _split_tool_calls(…)` (before any dedup/`contents.append`): `content, n = _strip_broken_tool_blocks(content)`; if `n`: accumulate, `_log`, and if `not content.strip()` set `content = \"\"`. After `content = \"\\n\\n\".join(…)`, before the 502 check: `if dropped and not content.strip() and not tool_calls: content = _BROKEN_BLOCK_NOTICE`. Strip is unconditional on `calls` (a batch with one valid and one broken block must not return the broken one in `content`). |\n229|| `_BROKEN_BLOCK_NOTICE` | module constant: `\"[opencode-zen-bridge: невалидный блок вызова инструмента отброшен]\"` — same family as the existing `[opencode-zen-bridge: …]` markers. |\n230|| Untouched | `_split_tool_calls`, `ToolCallParser._drain/_emit/_flush_all`, `_is_incomplete_tool_step`/`_incomplete_step_signal`, `_render_tool_call`, `_RequestAttempts`, retry caps, `held` flush in the stale snapshot. |\n231|\n232|### 4.5 `core/tool_emulation.py` and `bridges/muse-bridge/server.py` (AD-001, AD-003, AD-004)\n233|\n234|These keep strict decoding (D-08). Add, next to `_normalize_arguments` or `_parse_tool_call_block`:\n235|\n236|```python\n237|def _recover_trailing_braces(text: str) -> dict | None:      # same body as 4.1 but JSONDecoder() strict, no _log\n238|def _loads_tolerant(text: str) -> Any:\n239|    try:\n240|        return json.loads(text)\n241|    except ValueError:\n242|        recovered = _recover_trailing_braces(text)\n243|        if recovered is None:\n244|            raise\n245|        return recovered\n246|```\n247|and in `_parse_tool_call_block` replace `json.loads(_strip_code_fence(inner))` with `_loads_tolerant(_strip_code_fence(inner))`, then add the §4.2 unwrap. No other symbol changes (`_split_tool_call_inner`, `_parse_tool_call_blocks`, `ToolCallParser`, muse `strict_live`/`LiveParserError` semantics untouched). muse's `_parse_tool_call_block` is reachable under `strict_live=True`: a recovered block is a valid call, so no `LiveParserError` is raised for it; truly broken blocks keep raising.\n248|\n249|---\n250|\n251|## 5. High-Load Architecture Gates\n252|\n253|HL-ENV: the 46-field envelope is **inherited unchanged** from handoff §3 (local single-user stdlib bridge, `ThreadingHTTPServer`, ≤16 in-flight, 5 RPS peak). Deltas introduced by this design: CPU +≤2 ms worst case per request on cold paths, +0 allocations on hot path, +0 deps, +0 shared state, +0 I/O. The `C-MULT-I*`/`S-HERD-I*`/`R-BULK-I*` formulas about shared dependency pools (Redis/DB/GigaRC, fork/reload, singleflight) have no subject here: no new dependency is introduced; each gate below states the bound that does apply.\n254|\n255|### C-MULT/v1 — call multiplicity & retry amplification\n256|- Before: initial + ≤`NATIVE_RETRY_LIMIT`(=2) incomplete-step retries ⇒ **A_max = 3** upstream spawns per client call (live also enforces `MAX_TOTAL_SPAWNS=3`).\n257|- After: incident class resolves at attempt 1 ⇒ **1 spawn**. New code adds **0** spawns, **0** retries; retry triggers still read the *raw* `attempt_texts`, so A_max is unchanged at 3 in the worst case.\n258|- Parser work is in-process, O(len(block)); no hop.\n259|\n260|### S-HERD/v1 — stampede / shared-state contention\n261|- No new module-level mutable state: `_RAW_CALL_RE` is an existing compiled constant; helpers are pure; `dropped_blocks` is a per-request local cell. No locks.\n262|- Burst of 8 parallel turns each re-sanitising ≤256 KiB history: fast path is one `re.search` (sub-ms). Poisoned history is cleaned once per replay, which removes the cause of repeated re-prompt loops across turns.\n263|\n264|### H-CPU/v1 — hot-path CPU & complexity\n265|- Recovery runs only after two failed `json.loads` calls (cold). `raw_decode` O(n) + tail `str.strip` O(tail); no regex backtracking. 60 KiB: ≈0.23 ms measured (budget 5 ms p95).\n266|- `_strip_broken_tool_blocks`: fast path O(n) search; slow path O(k·n) because `_code_context` is O(n) per candidate ⇒ **k capped at `_STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS = 16`** (worst case ≤ 16·n; one 60 KiB broken block measured 1.97 ms; the capped worst case is covered by `test_strip_scan_is_bounded`). Remainder beyond the cap is left untouched (fail-open).\n267|- `VER-004` enforces `< 5 ms` for: parse of 60 KiB with `}}}`, parse of 60 KiB unterminated, strip of a 60 KiB broken block.\n268|\n269|### R-BULK/v1 — bulkhead, isolation, fault containment\n270|- Everything is request-thread-local; `ToolCallParser` is per attempt; no shared buffers. Parser buffer cap `_MAX_BUFFER = 65536` is untouched.\n271|- Failure matrix (single dependency = the helper itself): `RecursionError`/`ValueError` inside block parse ⇒ treated as \"not parseable\" (block dropped), never propagated; strip cap reached ⇒ fail-open + one log line; helper returns text unchanged on no match. No new timeout, retry, or breaker; existing `_RequestAttempts` breaker/budget/`MAX_TOTAL_SPAWNS` stay the only limiters.\n272|- Blast radius of a bug in the helper: assistant text content only (tool-call path `on_tool_call` is not routed through it).\n273|\n274|---\n275|\n276|## 6. Quality scenarios\n277|\n278|| ID | Quality | Scenario | Measure |\n279||---|---|---|---|\n280|| QA-001 | reliability | Model emits the production block with `}}}` (escaped and raw-newline heredoc variants) during `incomplete_tool_step re-prompt 1/2` | exactly 1 `bash` tool call; 0 raw `<tool_call>/<tool_invoke>` in SSE/JSON content or re-prompt; 1 upstream spawn |\n281|| QA-002 | performance | 60 KiB block with trailing braces / unterminated / broken-block strip | each < 5 ms (p95 budget; measured ≤ 2 ms) |\n282|\n283|## 7. Boundaries, contract delta, risks\n284|\n285|- **BND-001** `opencode-zen-bridge/server.py` parser/sanitizer layer: pure helpers + three sinks. Forbidden: modifying `_split_tool_calls` / `ToolCallParser` emit semantics; I/O or global mutation in helpers; changing `_render_tool_call`.\n286|- **BND-002** `core/tool_emulation.py`, `muse-bridge/server.py`: only `_parse_tool_call_block` + the local helper. Forbidden: cross-bridge/`core` imports from bridges, touching `ToolCallParser`/`strict_live`, adding lenient control-char decoding.\n287|- **CD-001** (behavior): producers = the three parsers/handlers; consumers = OpenAI-compatible clients (opencode, DSH) and the model. Accepts previously rejected inputs (trailing `}`, OpenAI envelope); stops returning rejected raw tool tags in assistant content; may return `_BROKEN_BLOCK_NOTICE`. No schema/field/status change. Required by REQ-002 of this task.\n288|- **RISK-001** (low/medium): recovery accepts an over-closed envelope that the model \"meant\" differently. Mitigation: dict-only, tail strictly whitespace+`}` (`, \"x\": 1}` tails are rejected), arguments still must be a dict, log line `tool_call_recovered`.\n289|- **RISK-002** (low/low-medium): residual or over-strip — (a) scan cap leaves tags in pathological text; (b) an unquoted unparseable tag example in prose is dropped; (c) first-attempt behaviour changes (D-07). Mitigation: quoted/fenced/valid preserved, cap + log, notice instead of empty reply, history sanitizer as second line, targeted tests.\n290|\n291|## 8. Verification surface (frozen)\n292|\n293|All commands run from the repo root after Coder step 0 (§9).\n294|\n295|| ID | Command | Expected |\n296||---|---|---|\n297|| VER-001 | `python3 -m unittest tests.test_tool_parser -v` | exit 0; includes new cross-bridge cases (trailing `}}}`/`}}}}\\n`, OpenAI `function` wrapper, name-wins, broken stays broken) for `core` and `muse`; ≥ 44 + new tests |\n298|| VER-002 | `cd bridges/opencode-zen-bridge && python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .` | exit 0 **or** failure set exactly equals the baseline set recorded at step 0 (`.ai-team/runs/<run>/receipts/baseline-failures.txt`; currently the 3 `test_unmapped_*` tests, D-09); test count = baseline + new; 0 errors |\n299|| VER-003 | `cd bridges/opencode-zen-bridge && python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t . -k negative_control -k unparsed_block_returned_as_text -k closed_batch_without_intermediate_close_kept -k sanitize_closed_alt_batch_kept -k broken_block -k history_renders_tool_calls` | exit 0; Ran ≥ 6; F-07 negative controls, kept-batch sanitizer tests and `\"id\"` rendering all green |\n300|| VER-004 | `cd bridges/opencode-zen-bridge && python3 -c \"import json,sys,time; sys.path.insert(0,'.'); import server as s; ok=json.dumps(dict(name='bash',arguments=dict(command='x'*60000))); big=ok+'}}}'; bad=ok[:-4]; blk='<tool_invoke>'+bad+'</tool_invoke>'; f=lambda fn,a: (lambda t: ([fn(a) for _ in range(20)], (time.perf_counter()-t)/20*1000)[1])(time.perf_counter()); a=f(s._parse_tool_call_blocks,big); b=f(s._parse_tool_call_blocks,bad); c=f(s._strip_broken_tool_blocks,blk); print(round(a,3),round(b,3),round(c,3)); sys.exit(0 if s._parse_tool_call_blocks(big) and s._parse_tool_call_blocks(bad) is None and s._strip_broken_tool_blocks(blk)==('',1) and max(a,b,c)<5 else 1)\"` | exit 0, three timings < 5 ms (pre-flight on the prototype: 0.23 / 0.16 / 1.97 ms) |\n301|\n302|### Test plan (REQ-004 → names the Coder must create; VER-003 `-k` relies on `broken_block`)\n303|\n304|`bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/tests/test_lenient_tool_call.py`\n305|- `test_trailing_braces_recovered` (`}`, `}}`, `} }\\n}`; production payload escaped **and** raw-newline) · `test_trailing_garbage_not_recovered` (`}}, \"x\": 1}`, non-dict, under-closed, `{broken`) · `test_openai_function_wrapper` (+ with extra `}`, name-wins, present-but-blank name still rejected) · `test_batch_segment_with_extra_brace`.\n306|\n307|`bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/tests/test_step_interruption.py`\n308|- `test_strip_broken_blocks_helper` (closed-invalid dropped, unclosed tail dropped, valid single/batch kept byte-identical, inline/fenced quoted kept, cap behaviour) · `test_sanitize_strips_malformed_closed_tool_invoke` + the two existing kept-batch tests · `test_incomplete_prompt_has_no_broken_block` · stream: `test_stream_broken_block_not_in_sse_nor_reprompt` (attempt 1 emits `<tool_invoke>{broken</tool_invoke>`; assert no raw tag in any SSE `content`, re-prompt 2 prompt has no tag, ≤ caps) · `test_stream_recovered_trailing_braces_single_spawn` · `test_stream_notice_when_only_broken_block` · json: `test_serve_json_broken_block_stripped_and_notice`, `test_serve_json_mixed_valid_and_broken` (call returned, broken not in `content`) · `test_strip_scan_is_bounded` (1000 broken tags, < 50 ms).\n309|\n310|`tests/test_tool_parser.py` (root)\n311|- Extend `TestCrossBridgeParserContract._contract_cases` with `trailing_braces`, `trailing_braces_ws`, `openai_function_wrapper`, `name_wins_over_function`, `malformed_stays_text`; plus `TestTrailingBraceRecovery` calling `core.tool_emulation` and the muse module directly (reuse `_load_muse_bridge`).\n312|\n313|Existing tests that must stay untouched and green: `test_negative_control_garbage_still_text_and_logged`, `test_unparsed_block_returned_as_text`, `test_closed_batch_without_intermediate_close_kept`, `test_sanitize_closed_alt_batch_kept`, `test_history_renders_tool_calls_and_results`, `test_malformed_member_rejects_whole_batch_as_text`.\n314|\n315|## 9. Evolution, rollout, rollback\n316|\n317|- **Compatibility:** additive tolerance + removal of raw rejected tags from content; OpenAI SSE/JSON schema, headers, status codes, `state/*.json` unchanged.\n318|- **Coder step 0 — re-baseline (mandatory, before any edit):** `bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/` is git-untracked; replace its `server.py`, `tests/` (incl. `dsh_tools_fixture.json`, `fixtures/`), `zen_catalog.py`, `sync_dsh_models.py`, `opencode-go.json`, `pyproject.toml` with the current `~/.dsh/bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/` copies **without** `state/`, `logs/`, `workspace/`; record `shasum -a 256 server.py` as `BASELINE_SHA` and run VER-002 once to record `baseline-failures.txt`. Re-resolve all anchors by symbol.\n319|- **Rollout:** (1) VER-001..004 green on the re-baselined copy; (2) immediately before deploy compare `shasum -a 256 ~/.dsh/bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py` with `BASELINE_SHA` — equal ⇒ copy; different ⇒ `git merge-file` / `patch` the Coder's diff onto the new live, re-run VER-001..004 on the merged result; never overwrite blindly; (3) back up the live file to `~/work/backups/` (workspace-paths canon, not beside the file); (4) `launchctl kickstart -k gui/501/com.user.dsh-opencode-zen-bridge`; (5) heavy-path check: a real tool-call turn on `127.0.0.1:9883` with a model that emits the `}}}` form (or a fake-CLI replay), plus `grep` of `bridge.err.log` for `tool_call_recovered` / `stream dropped`; core/muse ship via normal MR (they are tracked files).\n320|- **Rollback:** restore the backed-up `server.py` and `kickstart` (< 2 s); core/muse via `git revert`. Trigger: any new test failure vs. baseline set, crash on `:9883`, non-200, or a raw `<tool_invoke>` in live content.\n321|- **Feature flag:** none (not a GigaRC service, per handoff); the file-restore rollback is the kill switch.\n322|\n323|## 10. Coder constraints\n324|\n325|- Protected (read-only for Coder): `analysis/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/handoff-architect.md`, `analysis/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/evidence-ledger.md`, the frozen verification surface in the packet.\n326|- Do not change: anything in the \"Untouched\" row of §4.4; `_normalize_arguments`; strictness of core/muse decoders; retry caps; `_render_tool_call`.\n327|- Commit/process rules of the repo canon apply (regression tests before fix, Conventional Commits with `[agent]` tag, full suite before MR). `bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/` is untracked: its change ships through the live-patch procedure above, core/muse/tests through MR.\n328|\n329|## 11. Questions for the owner / orchestrator (class МОЖНО ПРОДОЛЖИТЬ — design is complete under the stated assumptions)\n330|\n331|- **Q-A (baseline):** live `~/.dsh/bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py` carries 3 pre-existing test failures (live now caps spawns at 3; the tests expect 4/2) and is evidently under active edit by another session. Assumption used: the Coder re-baselines on live, treats those 3 as baseline debt (neither fixes nor regresses them), and deploys as a patch. If the intended baseline is instead the stale d619 snapshot, only step 0 and the rollout guard change; the design does not.\n332|- **Q-B (scope, D-07):** sink filtering applies to the first attempt too (stricter than the handoff's \"retry only\"). Assumption: acceptable because the HL envelope states \"zero leaked raw tags\".\n333|- **Q-C:** `independent_review` is pre-set `PASS / arch-panel-pending / receipts/arch-panel.json` in the packet **by the orchestrator's brief**; that receipt does not exist yet and must be produced by the panel before `ARCH_GATE_PASS`.","final_result":true}}}
